  "raw": {
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006075": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant - Part-Time (26006075) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant - Part-Time (26006075) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant - Part-Time Dent Med-Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006075 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Dental Medicine is accepting applications for a part-time, appointment stream faculty position at the academic rank of Clinical Assistant Professor in the Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery at the commitment effort of one day per week. The faculty rank and salary will depend on experience and qualifications. The primary responsibility of this position would be: - Provide clinic coverage for pre-doctoral/resident students in Oral Maxillofacial Surgery - Teaching and clinic assignments will be at the chair’s discretion Applicants must have a DDS / DMD degree from an accredited school and a dental license to practice in the State of Pennsylvania. We are seeking candidates with significant clinical experience as an oral and maxillofacial surgeon and have graduated from an Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery residency program and must be board certified. The school is located on the University's main campus in Pittsburgh, contiguous with the other five health science schools. The School of Dental Medicine works as a key collaborative partner with the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC), an internationally renowned academic medical center and healthcare enterprise. The robust infrastructure supports clinicians and educators with innovative clinical programs, biomedical research, and health sciences research, enabling discoveries that save lives and change the landscape of patient care. As part of the clinical practice and faculty of the University of Pittsburgh, the practitioner will have the opportunity to collaborate with clinicians, innovators, and investigators from around the world and become part of a vibrant community of healthcare providers dedicated to making a difference in their chosen field and in the lives of others. To apply, please go to join.pitt.edu, select faculty positions, and search 26006075 in the keyword search. Please upload a curriculum vitae, and a statement describing your interest in the position, qualifications, and experience. The search committee will begin reviewing applications upon receipt.  Only applicants who appear best qualified will be invited for a personal interview. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005977": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant (26005977) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant (26005977) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant Chemistry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005977 ) The Department of Chemistry at the University of Pittsburgh invites applications for a full-time Visiting Research Assistant Professor to lead and conduct research on the chirality-induced spin selectivity (CISS) effect. The successful candidate will work closely with Professor Haitao Liu and his research group to investigate how molecular chirality governs spin-dependent electron transport and reactivity at surfaces and interfaces, with applications spanning spintronics, enantioselective electrochemistry and catalysis, and spin-controlled processes in molecular and biomolecular systems. Primary Responsibilities Design, execute, and interpret experiments probing spin-polarized charge transport through chiral molecules, self-assembled monolayers, and chiral thin films. Develop and apply surface- and interface-sensitive measurements relevant to CISS, which may include magnetoresistance and spin-dependent transport measurements, electrochemical methods (cyclic voltammetry, EIS, chronoamperometry), spin-polarized or magnetic-field-modulated electrochemistry, and characterization by AFM, XPS, QCM/QCM-D, ellipsometry, and related techniques. Prepare and characterize chiral molecular assemblies and substrates, including DNA-based and other biomolecular chiral systems where relevant. Author peer-reviewed publications and contribute to conference presentations and dissemination of results. Contribute to the preparation of grant proposals and reports to federal agencies and other sponsors. Mentor and train graduate and undergraduate researchers, and help maintain shared instrumentation and safe laboratory practices. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Chemistry, Physics, Materials Science, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research experience relevant to CISS, spin-dependent phenomena, electrochemistry, surface science, or molecular electronics, evidenced by a strong publication record. Hands-on expertise with one or more relevant experimental platforms (e.g., electrochemistry, surface characterization, magnetotransport, or spin-sensitive measurements). Ability to work independently, design rigorous experiments, and communicate results effectively in writing and in presentations. Preferred Qualifications Direct experience measuring or modeling the CISS effect or spin-polarized transport in molecular and solid state systems. Familiarity with chiral self-assembled monolayers, DNA nanostructures, or chiral inorganic/hybrid materials. Experience with instrument development, automation, or custom measurement setups. A record of successful collaboration across chemistry, physics, and materials science. Contributions to grant writing and evidence of emerging research independence. Appointment Terms This is a full-time, visiting research assistant professor appointment, the initial appointment term will be 1 year, with renewal contingent on performance and the availability of funding. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of research interests and experience (2–3 pages), and the names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation Optional Attachments : Research Statement Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005875": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005875) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005875) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005875 ) The Department of Pathology is recruiting an Assistant professor (5 years’ experience), Associate Professor (6-10 years of experience) or Professor (10+ years of experience) appointment stream, faculty position for the Division of Liver, Kidney, Cardiac, Small Bowel, and Transplantation Pathology. Experience in a large hospital-based native and allograft liver and kidney pathology service is desirable. The successful candidate will contribute to varied divisional diagnostic, research, and educational activities. The position will be responsible for reporting on allograft and native liver, heart, small bowel, and kidney biopsies. Academic development will focus on scientific areas related to clinical interests and responsibilities. The division is fully equipped to study spatial and general tissue proteogenomic profiling, multiplex labeling, image analysis, and practical AI applications related to clinical responsibilities. Interest in these areas is an advantage; unique opportunities exist to participate in multicenter study tissue analyses using the above approaches. Qualifications: Candidates must possess: · M.D degree · Board certification in Anatomic Pathology · Eligibility for Pennsylvania medical licensure is required Preferred qualifications include: · Fellowship training in a relevant pathology subspecialty Salary and benefits: · Salary will commensurate with experience · Full-time faculty member at the University of Pittsburgh as well as a participant in the UPMC/UPP faculty practice plan Please include (1) curriculum vitae; (2) a letter of interest describing research and academic interests, as well as (3) a brief statement of personal goals. For questions, please contact demetrisaj@upmc.edu or by mail at: Anthony J. Demetris, MD Director, Division of Liver, Kidney, and Transplantation Pathology UPMC Montefiore, Room E741 3459 Fifth Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15213 To apply: Go to TALENT CENTER at www.join.pitt.edu and search for requisition 26005875 in the keyword. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004389": {
      "title": "PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING",
      "description": "Job Description - PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING - School of Law (26004389) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING - School of Law (26004389) Job Description PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING - School of Law Law-Faculty - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004389 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Law invites applications for one or more full-time faculty positions at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Legal Writing. The position is part of a system of contracts progressing to presumptively renewable long-term contracts, separate from the University’s tenure stream. Pitt Law’s legal writing program develops the legal analytical skills of students and equips them to write and speak clearly and persuasively, in a manner appropriate for different audiences and purposes in law practice. The first-year Legal Analysis & Writing course spans two semesters, typically including “objective” writing assignments in the fall and persuasive writing assignments and oral argument in the spring. The course typically also encompasses related skill sets, including client interviewing and negotiation, among others. While the course covers the basics of legal research and includes open-resource assignments, students are separately required to take a one-credit course on the fundamentals of legal research, taught by library faculty, in the spring semester of their first year. Legal Writing faculty members typically teach two small sections of first-year Legal Analysis and Writing in the fall and spring (approximately 15-20 students per section), for a total of four credits for each section. They may also teach upper-level writing courses and may have some administrative duties. Legal Writing faculty have the opportunity to shape the future direction of the Legal Writing program and the law school more broadly as a full participant in faculty governance at Pitt Law. Minimum Requirements: J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school, excellent writing skills, and an outstanding academic record. Experience teaching legal writing and law practice experience are preferred. Candidates should be able to work effectively with a wide variety of students and have an interest in developing legal writing experiences for law students within a community that supports collaboration and innovative teaching. Candidates are encouraged to present their own ideas about teaching legal writing in an era of profound change and uncertainty in the legal profession and legal education, brought on by generative AI. Please provide a list of at least three (3) references with full contact information. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006061": {
      "title": "Faculty.Instructor.Instructor",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Instructor.Instructor - Part-Time (26006061) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Instructor.Instructor - Part-Time (26006061) Job Description Faculty.Instructor.Instructor - Part-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006061 ) The Division of General Internal Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh seeks an outstanding Part Time Instructor (appointment stream). The candidate will be co-developing and co-leading a course on Leading Interprofessional Education for the new PhD program within the Health Professions Education program at the Pitt ICRE. As we design the curriculum, it’s clear that strong expertise in interprofessional education and collaboration will be essential for preparing future scholars and leaders in health professions education. Effort allocation is 100% virtual teaching. General rank requirements: An Instructor should have demonstrated teaching ability and/or professional experience of a kind that would enable them to make an academic contribution. The Instructor should possess a doctoral or appropriate professional degree ( i.e. PharmD, PhD, MD). They should exhibit promise of originality and excellence in some field of scholarship and demonstrated ability in guiding and counseling students. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae for position #26006061 and apply using this link: http://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006096": {
      "title": "Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist (26006096) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist (26006096) Job Description Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist Falk School - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006096 ) Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist Falk Laboratory School, a coeducational K-8 school at the University of Pittsburgh, seeks a full-time educator to work with children who have a range of learning differences. This role begins January 2027 . Candidates must have empathy for, and a genuine interest in, developing positive educational experiences for students with learning differences. Among the professional duties of a Falk Learning Specialist are the following: Collaborate with staff members and families to create and implement intervention programs that maximize students’ access to the general education content Administer initial screening and diagnostic testing in both reading and mathematics to identify students who could benefit from remedial instruction Develop and teach motivating, engaging lessons that are grounded in best practices, and are appropriate to students’ ages, grade levels, and abilities Apply and support accommodations to support instruction Observe, evaluate, and prepare reports on students’ progress A Master of Education Degree in the field of special education or a related field is required. Broad experience in a school setting is advantageous as the position involves partnering across disciplines and grade levels. The minimum base salary is $50,000 (10-month contract); credit will be given for years of relevant experience. Falk Laboratory School, a department in the School of Education at the University of Pittsburgh, offers excellent benefits. Materials should be uploaded electronically to: https://www.join.pitt.edu/ . Please submit: 1.     Letter of application 2.     A resume 3.     An educational philosophy that includes a vision for an ideal experience for students with learning differences 4.     Three letters of recommendation 5.     Official transcripts 6.     PA instructional certificate or equivalent, if applicable Questions about the position can be sent to Dr. Joanna Newlin, jmn56@pitt.edu , Director of Student Services or Dr. Molly Hicks, Director of Administrative Operations, meh479@pitt.edu . Review of applications will begin mid-October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Offer of employment is contingent on the candidate satisfactorily obtaining and passing the following prior to commencement of appointment: Pennsylvania Department of Human Services Child Abuse History Clearance, Pennsylvania State Police Criminal Record Check and FBI Criminal Record Check. Also, as required by Act 168 of 2014, candidate must satisfy the requirements stated on the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Department of Education Sexual Misconduct/Abuse Disclosure Release Form. Proof of negative TB test required upon hire. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation, Teaching Statement, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005127": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005127) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005127) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005127 ) The Department of Medicine - The Division of General Internal Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking full-time faculty at the level of Assistant Professor in the appointment stream. Exciting opportunities are available for translational research and teaching. Qualified applicants must have a PhD in Health Professions Education and be an established investigator with a proven track record in research, teaching, and a strong publication record. The position offers superb opportunities for research, and teaching and mentoring of students, residents, and fellows. Academic appointments and salary are dependent upon qualifications and experience. The incumbent will contribute to the educational, research, and scholarly missions of the Institute through teaching, academic program leadership, and methodological consultation. They will teach five 1-credit courses, provide academic leadership as Assistant Director of the PhD Program in Health Professions Education and the Undergraduate Certificate in Clinical Research, and serve as a mixed-methods research expert supporting grant development across the Schools of the Health Sciences. Within the Center for Medical Education Research and Scholarship (CMERS), they will also provide methodological consultation to clinician educators, including curriculum, training, and program evaluation. Candidates for Assistant Professor in the appointment stream need three or more years of experience in related scientific research; have achieved or established the ability to attain external research funding; have dispersed results through peer-reviewed publications and other scientific forums; have noteworthy teaching experience; and established the capability for continued career development and promotion. We will continue to create and maintain an environment that allows individuals to discover, belong, contribute, and grow, while honoring the experiences, perspectives, and unique identities of all. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae and apply to requisition number 26005127 via: https://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005771": {
      "title": "Faculty Instructor",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Instructor - Part-Time OSHER (26005771) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Instructor - Part-Time OSHER (26005771) Job Description Faculty Instructor - Part-Time OSHER OSHER Lifelong Learning Institute - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005771 ) The Osher Lifelong Learning Institute (OLLI) at the University of Pittsburgh invites applications for part-time temporary faculty to teach non-credit courses of high interest, relevance, and timely topics to our OLLI members. Instructors will design and teach courses that engage mature learners who are aged 50 years or \"better.\" Courses are online or in person and will run approximately two hours weekly for five-week sessions scheduled for each academic term (fall, spring, and summer). Candidates must have submitted a course proposal that was reviewed and accepted by the OLLI curriculum committee. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005704": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005704) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005704) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005704 ) The Division of Rheumatology in the Department of Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh and UPMC are seeking an outstanding physician scientist at the Assistant Professor level (non-tenure track).  Physicians will be responsible for the management of patients with primary focus of working with dedicated scleroderma and Sjogren’s disease clinics, and corresponding observational cohort studies and clinical trials.   The physician will be responsible for both inpatient and outpatient cohorts of patients, will round at UPMC hospitals as assigned, and maintain at least six outpatient clinics per week and the continued care of those patients.  The physician will serve as a preceptor to fellows and residents and be involved in teaching at UPMC for trainees.  Physician will be 80% clinical, 10% research and 10% teaching. General rank requirements:  An Assistant Professor should have demonstrated teaching ability, experience in advanced study and research, or professional experience of a kind that would enable them to make an academic contribution.  The Assistant Professor should possess a doctoral or appropriate professional degree (MD or DO) and be Board Certified/Board Eligible.  They should exhibit promise of originality and excellence in some field of scholarship and should have demonstrated ability in guiding and counseling students.  To be appointed or promoted to an assistant professorship, a person should have the potential for promotion to Associate Professor. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae for position #26005704 and apply using this link: http://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004568": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26004568) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26004568) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004568 ) The Department of Medicine and Section of Palliative Care in the Division of General Internal Medicine is seeking a full-time physician (MD/DO), PhD scientist or PharmD in a relevant field with a research focus on palliative care and serious illness at the levels of Assistant Professor, appointment or tenure stream, Associate Professor, appointment or tenure stream and Professor, appointment stream or tenured depending on qualifications and career track to serve as the Associate Chief of Research (ACR) and Director of the Palliative Research Center (PaRC). In this role, the ACR will collaborate closely with the Section Faculty and report directly to the Section Chief. The Section of Palliative Care is a multidisciplinary team committed to improving quality of life for patients and families through delivery of quality palliative care, education of palliative care skills and advancement in palliative care innovation. We work with patients at academic hospitals and at outpatient clinics throughout the region. Our fellowship program is nationally recognized and comprised of four fellowship tracks to accommodate diverse career goals. The Palliative Research Center (PaRC) consists of faculty from across the Schools of Health Sciences, including researchers from palliative care and many medical subdisciplines, nursing, and public health. PaRC supports researchers throughout their careers and encourages collaboration between faculty members across disciplines. Key Responsibilities: Research Leadership – Develop and implement the strategic research mission of the Section and the Palliative Research Center (PaRC). Recruitment and Mentorship – Recruit junior and mid-level investigators and provide mentorship for palliative care investigators. Collaboration and Engagement – Promote synergy and partnerships across disciplines and University departments, schools and institutes. Grant Funding – Nurture collaborative relationships with foundations and industries and advance federal research projects (NIH, PCORI). Resources available: Palliative Research Center (PaRC) Center for Research on Health Care (CRHC) VA Center for Health Care Evaluation, Research Promotion (CHERP) Institute for Clinical Research Education (ICRE) Applicants for Assistant Professor, appointment or tenure stream, should have three or more years of experience in the field of clinical and/or health services research; have achieved or established the ability to attain external research funding; have dispersed results through peer-reviewed publications and other scientific forums; have noteworthy teaching experience; and established the capability for continued career development, promotion, and tenure. Applicants for Associate Professor, appointment or tenure stream, should have five or more years of experience in the field of clinical and/or health services research; have independent, external research funding and an extensive record of peer-reviewed publications; have substantial teaching experience; and demonstrate the ability for continued, impactful, independent scholarly contributions and leadership. Applicants for Professor, appointment stream or tenured, will have served five to seven years as Associate Professor. The rank of professor regards the individual accomplishments of respected knowledge and status in a distinguished ﬁeld of learning and the achievement of successful teaching knowledge and practices. The professor should have obtained enhanced stature in their ﬁeld through contributions of scholarship, professional practice, and leadership in professional and learning organizations. We offer a competitive salary, comprehensive benefits package, and a dynamic working environment. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae and apply to requisition number 26004568 via: https://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer/disability/veteran. About UPMC: The University of Pittsburgh and its partner, the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC), are committed to excellence in biomedical science and health care in southwestern Pennsylvania.  Together, they focus on training the next generation of health care specialists, conducting groundbreaking research, and delivering outstanding patient care.  The University encompasses six schools of health sciences, all sharing a mission to advance education, biomedical research, and health promotion.  Notably, the University has doubled its NIH support since 1998 and is a leader in NIH-funded institutions, underscoring its commitment to research infrastructure and faculty recruitment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
